essing.\n   - **Improvement Guidance:** Implement robust input validation for all user input fields when adding items. Ensure that names, descriptions, and prices cannot be empty before processing requests. Provide user feedback if validation fails.\n|Case|:**view_wishlist**\n   - **Error Analysis:** The expected wishlist item was not found on the page.\n   - **Improvement Guidance:** Ensure robustness in the mechanism that handles the persistence of wishlist items. Re-evaluate how items are added and removed from the wishlist, making sure the state is preserved correctly across user sessions.\n   - **Error Analysis:** The test fails because it expects items to be present in the user's wishlist, which may not have been added or persisted correctly due to previous failures in tests.\n   - **Improvement Guidance:** Focus on the integrity of data persistence between different operations such as adding items and viewing the wishlist. Consider implementing a rollback mechanism to restore initial states after each test. Make sure data consistency is preserved, so the system¡¯s state is predictable after any operation.\n", '|Case|:**remove_item_from_wishlist**\n   - **Error Analysis:** The attempt to locate an element for a non-existent item leads to a `NoSuchElementException`, which indicates that the script expected an item that was never added to the wishlist.\n   - **Improvement Guidance:** Implement checks for item existence before attempting to interact with UI elements directly. Ensure that the application gracefully handles situations where data does not exist, and specify behaviors in the interface for user clarity. Always manage the state and display accurate dynamically managed content so the user experience remains seamless.\n|Case|:**update_item_in_wishlist**\n   - **Error Analysis:** The updated item description is not reflected in the frontend, suggesting issues in either the update process or the data refresh logic.\n   - **Improvement Guidance:** Verify that the methods for manipulating the wishlist items (add, update, remove) are functioning as intended. Ensure that after any modification, the displayed data reflects the current state accurately by correctly saving and loading from the persistent data source. \n', '|Case|:**data_persistence**\n   - **Error Analysis:** The test fails because the "Logout" link cannot be found, likely due to the user never reaching the desired dashboard from a successful login state. This was likely caused by earlier test failures affecting the user\'s session.\n   - **Improvement Guidance:** Design tests to verify the presence of UI elements only after confirming navigational flow completes successfully. Use thorough assertions on session state before performing UI actions and check for all expected outputs at each stage of interaction. Plan your testing framework to ensure that user sessions and data states are appropriately managed and cleaned up after each test.']
